# training-atr-models — asteraix (130.92.59.242)
#
# Copy to .env. The unit reads it with EnvironmentFile=.
#
# IMPORTANT, and new since the split: until 16.09.2026 the gateway and the
# trainer read the SAME .env on one machine. They now read two files on two
# machines, and four values have to agree across them.
# They are marked >>> SHARED <<< below. The two paths break the handover
# silently when they disagree; the two keys fail loudly, with a 401 on the
# first call.

# ── who may call this host (#13) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two directions, two keys, and neither is the other (#9):
#   idhefix -> here   control: submit, read, cancel jobs   ATR_TRAIN_API_KEY
#   here -> idhefix   inference: promotion gate, eval/     ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_API_KEY
# This service reads no ATR_API_KEY at all; the gateway's key lives below, in the
# gateway section, under the name this service reads.
#
# >>> SHARED <<< with idhefix, under the SAME name there: the gateway reads its
# ATR_TRAIN_API_KEY and sends it as X-API-Key on every /train/* call. It must NOT
# be the gateway's ATR_API_KEY — a leaked caller key must not also start training
# runs here. Empty (as below): the service answers nothing but /health (503), and
# the launcher refuses the unit's 0.0.0.0 bind. Shorter than 32 characters: the
# same refusal. Generate it once and put the same line into both files:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
ATR_TRAIN_API_KEY=
# Who may connect besides loopback (always allowed): comma-separated IPs or
# CIDRs, no /0. This list is the ONLY source restriction on this host — ufw here
# does not filter high ports, and on 16.09.2026 a listener on :8299 was reached
# from idhefix and from a VPN client; nobody has sudo to add a rule. Empty admits
# loopback only, and the launcher refuses the 0.0.0.0 bind. idhefix, nothing else:
ATR_TRAIN_ALLOWED_CLIENTS=130.92.59.240
# A development switch for a loopback bind. Off, the launcher refuses the
# unit's bind and the service refuses every non-loopback caller. Leave it unset.
# ATR_TRAIN_REQUIRE_AUTH=true

# ── which host this is (#15) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every job this service accepts is stamped with this name, and it spawns,
# reconciles, cancels and counts on its card ONLY jobs carrying it: a pid means
# something on the machine that assigned it and nowhere else. Set it; the
# default is the hostname, and the hostnames are no identity — this box reports
# `dhserver03`, idhefix `srv` (measured 16.09.2026). Letters, digits, . _ - only.
# Changing it later orphans this host's live jobs: they would belong to a name
# nobody answers to. `ubelix` is refused — it marks the jobs Slurm supervises
# (ubelix/submit_job.py, fanout.py), which no trainer may start or signal.
ATR_TRAIN_HOST_ID=asteraix
# Whose a record WITHOUT a host is. All 48 in the shared store on 16.09.2026
# were written by the old trainer on idhefix, before the field existed. Leave
# the default (idhefix): set to this host, this service would judge idhefix's
# pids against its own /proc — the bug #15 is about.
# ATR_TRAIN_LEGACY_JOB_HOST=idhefix

# ── where the corpora and the trained weights live ───────────────────────────
# The research share, mounted on BOTH machines. That is what makes the handover
# cheap: the gateway on idhefix reads a path this host wrote, and the 48 job
# records written before the split are already readable here.
#
# !! Two trainers on this store: the code now prevents the double spawn and the
# false "failed" (#15) — each host judges only its own jobs, and a job is
# started only by whoever creates its claim file (O_CREAT|O_EXCL, exclusive
# across both machines on this share). BUT the old trainer on idhefix
# (serving-atr-inference) runs code WITHOUT that protection: it still marks
# every job whose pid is not alive on idhefix failed, and still starts any
# queued job it sees. So at cutover it must still be stopped AND disabled —
#   idhefix$ systemctl --user disable --now atr-train
# (disable, not only stop: WantedBy=default.target with linger brings it back
# at the next reboot) — BEFORE this host points at the shared store below.
# And only once no job is live on idhefix: this host never reconciles those,
# so after the stop nothing would. Nor does this host's /gpu-claim speak for
# idhefix's card — a gateway asking here sees no claim for such a run.
# Until then this host uses its own store, training_folder/jobs-asteraix.
ATR_TRAIN_JOBS_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/training_folder/jobs
# >>> SHARED <<< with idhefix — every registration's local_path is an absolute
# path under this directory, and the kraken engine on idhefix opens it as written,
# so the share must be mounted at the same path there. Since serving#138 a path
# that does not exist on idhefix is logged there and a request for the model
# fails naming it; before, resolve_weights took it for a DOI. It must be on the
# same filesystem as ATR_TRAIN_REGISTRY_ROOT below: a registration of weights
# anywhere else fails the job (the default, ~/atr-cache/trained, is local disk).
ATR_TRAIN_TRAINED_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/training_folder/trained
# A directory in there without metadata.json is removed (at startup and after a
# DELETE) only once it has not changed for this many hours and no live job of
# any host names it. A registration writes metadata.json LAST, so until then the
# other machine's model in progress looks exactly like an orphan. Minimum 1.
# ATR_TRAIN_ORPHAN_WEIGHTS_MIN_AGE_H=24

# ── what must NOT go on the share ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both of these are local *because the share broke them*, not as an optimisation:
#   checkpoints — the trainer saves via temp-file + rename, which is cross-device
#                 on CIFS (training/settings.py:43-50)
#   TMPDIR      — the datasets Arrow cache on the share cost one run 11½ hours
#                 (training/preflight.py:151-175)
# ATR_TRAIN_CHECKPOINT_ROOT defaults to ~/atr-cache/checkpoints; leave it local.
TMPDIR=/home/tobias/atr-cache/tmp

# ── the artefact cache (#109) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local disk, 100 GB budget. Note that it does NOT follow the data: the same
# share gives this host the same ground truth and the same HF cache, but a COLD
# artefact cache — the compile per selection is paid once more here.
# ATR_TRAIN_ARTEFACT_CACHE_ROOT=/home/tobias/atr-cache/artefacts

# ── the model registry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# >>> SHARED <<< — MUST equal ATR_REGISTRY_ROOT in the gateway's .env on idhefix.
# One directory, two directions (serving-atr-inference#138):
#   models.yaml        the gateway PUBLISHES it; this host reads it, and only
#                      kraken does, to resolve a base_model given as a registry id
#   trained/<id>.yaml  this host WRITES one per trained model (#14); the gateway
#                      serves them without a restart
# A mismatch fails no request: models register into a directory the gateway
# never reads, and base models resolve against a file it never publishes. Since
# #14 a job whose registration cannot be written FAILS, naming where the weights
# are — but a wrong directory that happens to exist is written to happily.
# The default in settings.py is already this path; it is repeated here because
# it is one of the values that must agree across the two machines.
ATR_TRAIN_REGISTRY_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/registry
# The curated file is derived from the root (<root>/models.yaml). Do not set it
# alongside: two settings naming one place drift apart. An empty value is unset.
# ATR_TRAIN_MODELS_CONFIG=

# ── the gateway on idhefix ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two of the three HTTP edges across the seam point here: the promotion gate
# (training/promote.py) and, after the move, eval/. No longer loopback.
ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_URL=http://130.92.59.240:8200
# The gateway reads trained/ at most every ATR_REGISTRY_RELOAD_INTERVAL_S (5 s),
# so the gate's first request after a registration is "404 unknown model". It
# asks again every 10 s for up to 90 s. Keep the spacing above that interval.
# ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_REGISTRY_WAIT_S=90
# ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_REGISTRY_RETRY_S=10
# >>> SHARED <<< — the gateway's own ATR_API_KEY from idhefix's .env, under this
# name here. The promotion gate presents it to :8200. Not ATR_TRAIN_API_KEY
# above, which guards the other direction.
ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_API_KEY=replace-with-the-ATR_API_KEY-from-idhefix

# ── the HF hub cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT set here, and that is deliberate: ~/.cache/huggingface/hub is a symlink to
# /mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/hf_hub (set 16.09.2026, write test
# passed), shared with the separate lassberg/vlm_training project. Setting
# HF_HOME would route around the symlink and re-download 6.6 TB.
#
# Open question, recorded rather than answered: two *projects* already write that
# cache; two *hosts* is untested. The documented CIFS issue is dedup, explicitly
# "harmless but not optimal" — not concurrency.
# HF_HOME=   <- leave unset

# ── bind and card ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The bind is NOT set here: deploy/systemd/atr-train.service passes
# --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8204 on its command line, so widening or narrowing it is
# an edit in git, never one quiet line in this file. Since #13 that bind reaches
# beyond loopback, and the launcher it runs (python -m atr_training.serve)
# refuses it — exit 2, naming what is missing, not retried by systemd — unless
# this file holds all three of ATR_TRAIN_REQUIRE_AUTH (true, the default),
# ATR_TRAIN_API_KEY (32+ characters) and ATR_TRAIN_ALLOWED_CLIENTS (non-empty).
# `bash scripts/install_user_unit.sh` asks the launcher before installing.
# ATR_TRAIN_HOST / ATR_TRAIN_PORT only set the launcher's defaults when it is
# started by hand; the unit overrides both.
#
# The card a job runs on, as a PHYSICAL index (nvidia-smi's numbering). Both A40s
# here are free and NVLinked; per-job allocation is #12.
ATR_TRAIN_GPU=1
